        "original_id": "7b4def5c-92f9-5121-8664-a7208d583a4b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Oscar Hammerstein II, Jerome Kern\n- Works: “Mis'ry's Comin' Aroun,” “Show Boat”\n- Roles: librettist, theatrical producer, theatre director\n- Awards: Tony Awards, Academy Awards\n\nFacts:\n- In 1927, Jerome Kern and Oscar Hammerstein II created the musical “Show Boat.”\n- “Mis'ry's Comin' Aroun” is a song from the 1927 musical “Show Boat” that was once neglected.\n- Oscar Greeley Clendenning Hammerstein II was born on July 12, 1895, and died on August 23, 1960.\n- Oscar Hammerstein II was an American librettist, theatrical producer, and usually uncredited theatre director of musicals for almost forty years.\n- Oscar Hammerstein II won eight Tony Awards and two Academy Awards for Best Original Song.",
